From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: 991 - settle dynbh upgrade loop for a non-best-band leaf

dynbh_upgrade_backhaul_cb only settles when the agent has a downstream child
or its connected band equals the best configured bSTA priority. A leaf agent
whose only reachable backhaul band is not the highest-priority one (e.g. a
2-hop Pro-8X that cannot reach the priority-0 band) satisfies neither, so it
keeps entering the upgrade path and re-enables + rescans every bStas each
cycle. That undoes the on-connect disable of the non-uplink bStas, which then
stay enabled-but-unassociated and, via mt76 apsta follow-sta, hold their
radios in retry_setup_failed -- collapsing the AP-MLD to a single flapping
link and intermittently dropping the fronthaul SSID.

Also settle once the bounded upgrade attempts are exhausted (dynbh_attempts>=3,
the existing give-up signal). dynbh_bh_lost resets dynbh_attempts=0 and
re-enables all bStas on real uplink loss, so failover and rescanning are
preserved; nodes that can reach the best band settle via the existing clauses
before attempts ever climb.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/backhaul.c
+++ b/src/backhaul.c
@@ -279,6 +279,14 @@
 	/* exceptions for which triggering dynbh is not relevant */
 	if ((agent_has_downstream(a) && !a->dynbh_upgrade_ongoing) ||
 	    (best && (best->cfg->priority == best_prio) && !a->dynbh_upgrade_ongoing) ||
+	    /* 991: a leaf agent whose reachable band is not the best-priority
+	     * one never settles here (no downstream, prio mismatch), so the
+	     * upgrade loop re-enables+rescans every bStas each cycle, undoing the
+	     * on-connect disable and stalling the non-uplink radios (mt76
+	     * follow-sta -> retry_setup_failed). Settle once the bounded upgrade
+	     * attempts are exhausted; dynbh_bh_lost resets attempts=0 on real
+	     * uplink loss, so failover/rescan is preserved. */
+	    (best && a->dynbh_attempts >= 3 && !a->dynbh_upgrade_ongoing) ||
 	    agent_is_backhaul_type_eth() || a->cfg.backhaul_override ||
 	    !agent_is_bsta_onboarded(a)) {
 		timer_set(&a->dynbh_scheduler, timeout * 1000);
